SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian Rhetoric Ahead of Attack Against Ukraine: Deny, Deflect, Mislead","publisher":"FactCheck.org","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.factcheck.org/2022/02/russian-rhetoric-ahead-of-attack-against-ukraine-deny-deflect-mislead/","claim":"Putin and Kremlin officials repeatedly denied that Russia planned to invade Ukraine while calling Russia peaceful and saying it would not attack anyone; the article says that denial was proven false by the full-scale invasion on February 24.","locator":"lines 72-75","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous fact-check with direct quotations and immediate outcome confirmation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution: it quotes Putin and his spokesman as the speakers of the false denial campaign.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin and Russian officials made the denials at the time."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vladimir Putin repeats false claim of genocide in Ukraine","publisher":"PolitiFact","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://www.politifact.com/factchecks/2022/feb/25/vladimir-putin/putin-repeats-long-running-claim-genocide-ukraine/","claim":"PolitiFact says Putin repeated a false genocide claim in his February 24 address, and that there is no evidence supporting the claim that ethnic Russians in Ukraine faced genocide.","locator":"lines 124-127","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Fact-check built around the president’s own speech and corroborating international evidence.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution: the false claim is Putin’s own public justification for war.","contrary_evidence":["Putin and Russian officials have long repeated the genocide allegation."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vladimir Putin's false war claims","publisher":"Deutsche Welle","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://amp.dw.com/en/fact-check-do-vladimir-putins-justifications-for-going-to-war-against-ukraine-add-up/a-60917168","claim":"DW says Putin’s stated reasons for war - including denazifying Ukraine and acting in self-defense - were false propaganda claims with no basis.","locator":"lines 90-104","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous fact-check with direct quotation of the speech and specific falsity determinations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution: Putin personally advanced the false justifications in a public address.","contrary_evidence":[],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin's False Claim of Self-Defense While Starting a War on Ukraine","publisher":"Voice of America","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.voanews.com/a/fact-check-putin-ukraine-war/6743290.html","claim":"VOA quotes Putin saying he launched a special military operation to protect people from genocide and to demilitarize Ukraine, then labels the self-defense claim false because no one attacked Russia.","locator":"lines 96-105","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"It reproduces Putin’s own statement and immediately evaluates it against the Charter and the facts on the ground.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution: this is Putin’s own war justification, rebutted in the same item.","contrary_evidence":["Putin’s statement itself framed the invasion as self-defense."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's attack on Ukraine came after months of denials it would attack","publisher":"The Washington Post","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/2022/02/24/ukraine-russia-denials/","claim":"The Post reports that Russian officials spent weeks denying plans to attack Ukraine, ridiculing warnings as hysteria and fairy tales, before the full-scale assault began.","locator":"lines 29-33","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report summarizing a broad denial campaign immediately contradicted by events.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution to Putin’s governing line, though the article notes some uncertainty about whether the denials were deliberate disinformation or closed decision-making.","contrary_evidence":["The article notes it is not clear whether the denials were deliberate disinformation or closed-off decision-making."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"World Court: Ukraine has filed suit against Russia, citing false genocide claims","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-02-27","url":"https://uk.investing.com/news/world-news/world-court-ukraine-has-filed-suit-against-russia-citing-false-genocide-claims-2593677","claim":"Reuters reports that the International Court of Justice confirmed Ukraine’s case and said Russia’s claim that it invaded to prevent genocide is false.","locator":"lines 407-408","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters summary of an ICJ filing and the court’s confirmation; strong corroboration, though still mediated reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong indirect attribution: the false genocide rationale is Putin’s and Russia’s public justification for the invasion.","contrary_evidence":["Russia publicly maintained the genocide justification."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin tells Russian business people he had no choice over Ukraine","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/putin-tells-russian-business-people-he-had-no-choice-over-ukraine-2771505","claim":"Putin told business leaders he had no other option but to order the operation against Ukraine and said Moscow had been forced into action.","locator":"lines 418-422","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct Reuters report on a televised meeting and Putin’s own words.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong direct attribution: these are Putin’s own public statements explaining the invasion.","contrary_evidence":[],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.8","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Why the U.S. is targeting Putin's daughters Katerina and Maria","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-04-06","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/why-the-us-is-targeting-putins-daughters-katerina-and-maria-2799414","claim":"Reuters reports that U.S. officials believed Putin’s adult daughters were hiding his wealth, and that Maria Vorontsova led government-funded programs personally overseen by Putin.","locator":"lines 430-436","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters quotes U.S. officials and ties the family to state-funded programs; the wealth claim is still inferential rather than admitted.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the report ties concealment and benefits to Putin’s daughters and explicitly says officials believed the wealth was hidden with family members.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin said it was bewildered by the sanctions and denied hidden family assets."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.5","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UK sanctions target the lavish lifestyles of Putin’s daughters","publisher":"GOV.UK","publication_date":"2022-04-08","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/news/uk-sanctions-target-the-lavish-lifestyles-of-putins-daughters","claim":"The UK government said it sanctioned Putin’s daughters, described the Kremlin inner circle’s lavish lifestyles, and stated that more than £275 billion of Putin’s war chest had been frozen.","locator":"lines 77-100","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official sanctions notice with named designations and stated basis.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the action targets Putin’s family and the wider elite he governs.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin rejected the broader sanctions framing."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"U.S. Treasury Escalates Sanctions on Russia for Its Atrocities in Ukraine","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-04-06","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0705","claim":"Treasury said it was targeting family members of President Vladimir Putin as part of sanctions imposed in response to Russia’s war against Ukraine.","locator":"lines 607-611","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official OFAC sanctions notice with explicit designation rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the sanctions are expressly aimed at Putin’s family and war support network.","contrary_evidence":[],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treasury Sanctions Kremlin Elites, Leaders, Oligarchs, and Family for Enabling Putin’s War Against Ukraine","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2022-03-11","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jy0650","claim":"Treasury said three of Putin spokesperson Dmitry Peskov’s family members lived lifestyles incongruous with his salary and likely built on ill-gotten wealth from his connections to Putin, including a property empire worth more than $10 million.","locator":"lines 616-620","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official sanctions notice with unusually specific descriptions of the family wealth and its purported source.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the claim is about Putin’s spokesperson and the personal network around Putin, not a direct Putin self-confession.","contrary_evidence":["Peskov has publicly denied the asset claims in related reporting."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian Asset Tracker","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022-08-04","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/project/russian-asset-tracker","claim":"OCCRP said its final update documented more than $19.8 billion in assets owned by Russia’s rich and powerful and that the assets were tied through documentary evidence to Putin’s circle.","locator":"lines 42-44","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Large investigative compilation based on documentary tracing; strong for the existence of a hidden-asset network, though not every item is equally direct.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: it explicitly ties the asset network to Putin’s circle rather than to Russia in the abstract.","contrary_evidence":["Documentary tracing still does not prove every asset is personally owned by Putin."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.5","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian activists publish leaked photos of Putin-linked palace","publisher":"The Guardian","publication_date":"2022-01-21","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2022/jan/21/russian-activists-publish-leaked-photos-of-putin-linked-palace","claim":"Leaked photographs confirmed details of a luxurious palace allegedly built for Putin’s personal use, including a marble pool, hookah lounge, wine cellar and theatre.","locator":"lines 155-157","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Investigative reporting based on leaked photographs and prior anti-corruption work; the ownership claim remains alleged rather than admitted.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 pattern evidence still relevant to the 2022 ruler-period because it concerns an active personal-wealth allegation around Putin.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the property is reported as Putin-linked and allegedly for his personal use, but the Kremlin denied ownership.","contrary_evidence":["The Russian president denied that the residence was built for his personal use."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"ICIJ’s guide to Russian wealth hidden offshore","publisher":"ICIJ","publication_date":"2022-04-20","url":"https://www.icij.org/investigations/russia-archive/icijs-guide-to-russian-wealth-hidden-offshore/","claim":"ICIJ said its reporting had revealed hidden financial networks of oligarchs, businesses, frontmen and professionals who backed Vladimir Putin’s rise to power, and that much of Russia’s ruling-elite wealth is hidden offshore.","locator":"lines 71-73","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"High-quality investigative summary grounded in prior ICIJ leaks and reporting, though it synthesizes rather than adjudicates ownership in each case.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 pattern evidence relevant to the 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the guide explicitly links the offshore networks to Putin’s rise and his inner circle.","contrary_evidence":["ICIJ notes that presence in offshore leaks does not by itself prove illegality."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.5","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"How a network of enablers have helped Russia’s oligarchs hide their wealth abroad","publisher":"ICIJ","publication_date":"2022-03-02","url":"https://www.icij.org/investigations/russia-archive/how-a-network-of-enablers-have-helped-russias-oligarchs-hide-their-wealth-abroad/","claim":"ICIJ said elites close to Vladimir Putin funneled billions through tax havens to evade scrutiny and oversight, with lawyers, proxies and bankers making it possible.","locator":"lines 64-72","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Investigative synthesis of offshore records and leak-based reporting, strong on pattern and network behavior.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 pattern evidence relevant to the 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the wealth-hiding network is explicitly described as being close to Putin.","contrary_evidence":["The item describes network behavior; it is not a direct admission by Putin."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.7","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"We Cannot Use It: Leaked E-Mails Show How Russian Petrochemical Giant Sibur Paid For Villa Linked to Putin","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022-06-20","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/project/russian-asset-tracker/we-cannot-use-it-leaked-e-mails-show-how-russian-petrochemical-giant-sibur-paid-for-villa-linked-to-putin","claim":"OCCRP said leaked emails showed Sibur spent large sums on Villa Sellgren, a mansion on the Gulf of Finland reported as a Putin vacation destination, and that employees did not understand why the money was being spent.","locator":"lines 68-73","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Document-backed investigative reporting with leaked emails and corroborating prior reporting.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year and tied to a long-running Putin-linked property pattern.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the property is reported as Putin-linked and the funding flowed through a company long associated with him and his family.","contrary_evidence":["The company and associated actors did not publicly explain the spending as ordinary business necessity."],"lenses":["7B.4","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin's Friend Receives State Funding to Combat Corruption","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2019-01-15","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/news/putins-friend-receives-state-funding-to-combat-corruption","claim":"OCCRP reported that Arkady Rotenberg, a childhood friend of Putin, won a state contract for anti-corruption training, and that Putin had earlier created a state body that handed Rotenberg control over part of the vodka market.","locator":"lines 32-52","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Older investigative reporting with concrete state-contract and ownership details that are directly relevant to patronage patterns.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 pattern evidence relevant to the 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the item concerns a childhood friend of Putin receiving state benefit through proximity to Putin.","contrary_evidence":[],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Cars, Connections, and Contracts in Putin’s Russia","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2016-03-31","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/investigation/cars-connections-and-contracts-in-putins-russia","claim":"OCCRP reported that companies with ties to Russia’s security and prosecutorial elite won large state contracts and that watchdogs described this as a common pattern where taxpayers’ money flows to those close to the elite.","locator":"lines 51-55","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Documentary investigative reporting showing a recurring conflict-of-interest pattern in the Putin-era state.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 pattern evidence relevant to the 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the article situates the contract pattern inside the Putin-era elite network.","contrary_evidence":[],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Leaked Emails Reveal How Putin’s Friends Dodged Sanctions With Help of Western Enablers","publisher":"OCCRP","publication_date":"2022-09-15","url":"https://www.occrp.org/en/project/the-rotenberg-files/leaked-emails-reveal-how-putins-friends-dodged-sanctions-with-help-of-western-enablers","claim":"OCCRP published leaked emails showing a memo labeled Objective: Clear Sanctions that described a restructuring plan to preserve the Rotenberg brothers’ share in Helsinki Halli.","locator":"lines 84-88","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct documentary leak with explicit sanctions-evasion planning.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year, though the conduct is rooted in earlier sanctions circumvention.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the brothers are long-time Putin associates, and the concealment behavior is tied to Putin’s orbit.","contrary_evidence":["The source relies on leaked emails and describes an alleged restructuring plan rather than a judicial finding."],"lenses":["7B.7","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treasury Sanctions Russian Officials, Members Of The Russian Leadership’s Inner Circle, And An Entity For Involvement In The Situation In Ukraine","publisher":"U.S. Department of the Treasury","publication_date":"2014-03-20","url":"https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/jl23331","claim":"Treasury said Putin has investments in Gunvor, that the Rotenberg brothers received about $7 billion in contracts awarded by Putin, and that Yuri Kovalchuk was Putin’s personal banker and cashiers-like advisor.","locator":"lines 648-653","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official sanctions notice with unusually explicit descriptions of the Putin inner circle’s financial and contract links.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-2022 pattern evidence relevant to the 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Indirect but strong: the notice directly ties financial benefit, contracts and access to Putin’s personal circle.","contrary_evidence":["This is a sanctions finding, not a criminal verdict; the government notice is itself an accusation-based instrument."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.5","7B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia: Fraud charges against Aleksei Navalny are arbitrary and politically motivated","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-03-11","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/documents/eur46/5329/2022/en/","claim":"Amnesty concluded that the new fraud charges against Navalny were politically motivated and aimed to criminalize his anti-corruption and political activism.","locator":"lines 67-68","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct human-rights assessment of a politically sensitive prosecution closely tied to anti-corruption scrutiny of the Putin system.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Strong indirect attribution: the prosecution targeted Navalny’s anti-corruption work against Putin-linked elites, but the item stops short of proving Putin personally ordered the charge.","contrary_evidence":["The Russian authorities presented the case as a legal fraud prosecution."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia: One year after jailing, Aleksei Navalny and his associates in a living hell","publisher":"Amnesty International","publication_date":"2022-01-17","url":"https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/news/2022/01/russia-one-year-after-jailing-aleksei-navalny-and-his-associates-in-a-living-hell/","claim":"Amnesty said Russian authorities dismantled Navalny’s Anti-Corruption Foundation, labelled his organizations extremist, blocked their websites, and criminalized their activities.","locator":"lines 64-71","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct human-rights reporting on state suppression of an anti-corruption movement with clear, traceable dates and actions.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year and immediately prior to the invasion period.","ruler_attribution":"Strong indirect attribution: the crackdown targeted the leading anti-corruption network challenging Putin’s circle, but the item does not itself prove direct personal orders.","contrary_evidence":[],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Navalnyy and Others v. Russia","publisher":"European Court of Human Rights","publication_date":"2022-10-04","url":"https://hudoc.echr.coe.int/app/conversion/docx/html/body?id=001-219557&library=ECHR","claim":"The court record notes that Navalny’s 2017 film alleged a high-ranking state official used charities and shell companies to amass luxuries, and that he brought an Article 18 political-ends complaint over his arrest and detention.","locator":"lines 37 and 83-84","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Judicial record from the European Court, directly describing the anti-corruption allegation and the political-purpose complaint.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective judicial evidence about a long-running pattern relevant to the 2022 ruler-period.","ruler_attribution":"Strong indirect attribution: the case concerns anti-corruption allegations against a high-ranking state official within the Putin system and state treatment of the investigator.","contrary_evidence":["The judgment addresses complaints and procedure; it is not a confession by Putin."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.10"]}

